From 0b5346b496097f22e54dddcdb9614fb724d93446 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:28:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/23] BananaDS perf: the compositor's step list kept while
 its inputs hold (render.2d_steps_cache)

BuildSteps made the painter's step list (which layer lines, in which order, from which one up) once per line, for
each unit: ~220 instructions a call (16 priority x BG tests, the sprite steps, the search for the covering layer),
83k instructions a frame on the 2D thread at 2x (dsstress L5), 86k on membench's emulator's thread at 1x, 138k on
ds2dtest: 2-3% of the thread, for the same answer on nearly every line.

The list now lives in the renderer (Steps[8]) with the key of everything BuildSteps reads: the layers drawn and
full, the sprite priorities present, the four BG priorities, the raw 3D path and whether a second pixel is wanted;
the layer lines, OBJColor and the backdrop are fixed buffers, and the raw 3D step's line (the one per-line input)
is set on every call either way. With render.2d_steps_cache (default on) a call whose key equals the last one's
returns the kept list; off, it is rebuilt every line as before. CompStep moves to the header for the member.

Exact by construction (the same inputs, the same list); checked by the matrix (m14) and the per-toggle A/B.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PvbFhKAw3ERk5a13S651g1
